sections.text:
All reports now run on one screen, **Reports → <report>** (`/main-sidebar/report-options/r/<key>`), with the same card design and list bar as before. The menu has 34 reports in five sections. The 11 old report screens still open by their old address but are no longer in the menu.

What every report now has (the 1.7.3 suggestions):
- one **Employee** column as "Full name (code)", and the same Branch / Department / Designation / Category columns;
- **rows limited on the server** to the user's branches and to the branches picked in the top bar (before, the old report files held every branch);
- a **Period** bar on reports with dates (This month, Last month, This quarter, This year, Last year, or any dates + Run), opening on a sensible default;
- **readable values** – Approved, Minor damage, Yes / No – and totals of the money and count columns above the table;
- **Favourites** in the Filters menu (on every list, not only reports): save the current filters and grouping under a name; saved per user and screen;
- **E-mail me**: sends the report, as filtered by period and branch, to the user's e-mail as a CSV file (company mail settings, else the fallback sender) – e.g. documents expiring this quarter;
- no duplicate controls: one Export (Excel / CSV / PDF), one set of filters; no Import.
- A user sees only the reports their role allows (each report needs one of the view rights listed below); ESS-only users see none.

| Section | Report | New | Needs one of |
|---|---|---|---|
| People | Employees (with form-designer fields, age, service, status) | updated | view_report, view_emp_master |
| | Headcount and turnover (by branch and department: male, female, joined, left, turnover %) | new | view_report, view_emp_master |
| | Joiners and leavers | new | view_report, view_emp_maste

- About 180 new Arabic texts. The employee page and list are fully right-to-left, and the side panel opens from the left.
- Dates and numbers keep their order inside Arabic text.
- On a phone:
  - the header wraps and the six groups become a row of tabs;
  - tables scroll sideways instead of turning into cards;
  - the side panel takes the full width.

- **Company industry types:**
  - added *Construction and engineering*, *Oil and gas* and *Property management*;
  - *Other* is now *General*;
  - these are choices only, so no table changes.
- **Default industry of each app:**
  - Property management → the property pack for CRM, Property and Maintenance;
  - Construction, Manufacturing, Healthcare, Oil and gas → the matching HSE pack;
  - anything else → the general pack.
- **Company creation:**
  - the company form has **Apps for this company** (HRMS ticked).
  - the ticked apps are activated with the company industry.
  - `setup_zeo` has `--apps hrms,projects,crm,property,maintenance,hse` and `--industry PM`.

- Each app's roles are permission groups named **"<App> – <role>"**. They are made when the app is activated (or with `setup_zeo` / `zeoapps_setup --roles`):
  - CRM: 4 groups;
  - Property: 7 groups;
  - Maintenance: 4 groups;
  - HSE: 16 groups;
  - Projects: 7 groups.
- You give them to users under **Settings → Users & rights**, exactly like the HRMS groups.
- **Settings → Permission groups** has a new **App** column.

- **Modules:** each new app has its own modules in the launcher, one per section, like Projects:
  - CRM: CRM home, Sales, Setup;
  - Property: Property home, Portfolio, Leasing & sales, Finance, Setup;
  - Maintenance: Maintenance home, Work, Planning, Setup;
  - HSE: My safety, Safety operations, Health & environment, Assurance & quality, Actions & claims, Setup.
- **Loading:** each app loads on first use, as Projects does.
- **Portal:** the Property tenant / owner / buyer portal is at `/prop-portal/login`.
- **Ask ZEO:** it answers HSE questions when HSE is active (incidents, permits, actions, audits…), with HSE suggestions in the HSE app. In CRM, Property and Maintenance, it says that it does not read those records yet.
- **Arabic:** 138 new texts – the menus, the launcher, Settings → Apps and the company form.

- **62 reports** of the new apps are in **Reports** with the HRMS report layout (period, filters, group by, totals, favourites, e-mail me, Excel / PDF):
  - CRM: Sales pipeline by stage, Won and lost by agent, Lead source effectiveness, plus a register report for each list;
  - Property: Occupancy by building, Rent roll, Aged receivables, plus registers;
  - Maintenance: Work orders by category and SLA, Technician workload, plus registers;
  - HSE: Incidents, Permits, Corrective actions, HSE performance by month, plus a report for every HSE register;
  - Projects: the 14 Projects reports.
- Each app's menu has a **Reports** module. Rows open their record.
- Reports of an app that is not active are not listed and cannot be run.

- **Leave request screen (HR, self service, HR for an employee):** the number comes from the branch's row in **Settings › Document numbering** (prefix, suffix, total length, counter). Checked on two branches:
  - the numbers follow on without gaps (`Q7C-LEA-0014`, `0015`, `0016`; `DXB-LEA-0007` …) and the counter equals the last number;
  - a rejected request keeps its number, and the next request gets a new one;
  - a number typed on the form is kept; the same number typed again is refused with a clear message (no server error);
  - four requests saved at the same moment get four different numbers.
- **Fixed – late-in / early-out penalties.** The penalty leave that attendance creates (when a policy deducts late or early days from a leave type) was saved **without a number**; the second penalty in a company then failed (*duplicate key*), so penalties stopped being deducted. A leave request saved without a number now takes the next number from its branch's setup. If the branch has no numbering row for leave requests, the save stops with *Set up document numbering for leave requests of branch …*.

Payroll → **Provisions**. A run per month holds, for every active employee, the liability at the month end and the change on the month before for:
- **Gratuity** (end of service) – the same amount as Reports → Gratuity;
- **Leave salary** – the same amount as Reports → Leave liability;
- **Air tickets** – the open air-ticket entitlements.

The run is made automatically on the 1st for the month before (Celery beat `payrollplus-provisions`) or any time with *Make / remake the month*. A run is *Draft*, then *Final*; **Post to accounting** (when the Accounting integration is on) sends the totals as the month-end provisions journal and marks the run *Posted*. **CSV** exports the lines for the accountant.

Attendance → Setup → **Overtime law and reasons** shows the overtime multipliers of the company country (Country pack) – normal, night, rest day and public holiday – with the law text:
- **AE** Decree-Law 33/2021 Art. 19: 1.25, night 1.50, rest day / holiday 1.50;
- **SA** Labour Law Art. 107: 1.50;
- **OM** RD 53/2023: 1.25, night 1.50, rest day / holiday 2.00;
- **QA** Law 14/2004 Art. 74: 1.25, night 1.50, rest day / holiday 1.50;
- **KW** Law 6/2010: 1.25, rest day 1.50, holiday 2.00;
- **IN** Factories Act s.59: 2.00.

*Put these rates on every attendance rule* writes them into the rules. An attendance rule without its own rate now uses the country rate (before: 1.25 everywhere). The employee's **My payslips** shows, for the month, the overtime hours by kind, the rate and the amount next to the overtime of the payslip.

Payroll → Salaries → **Payroll what-if**. A scenario has a name, the payroll month to compare and one or more changes:
- **Up / down by %**, **up / down by an amount**, **new amount** – for a salary component the employees already have;
- **Give it (new allowance)** – the employees get the component with the amount;
- for **everybody**, chosen **departments**, **branches**, **designations** or **employees**.

*Calculate* runs the month's payroll twice with the real payroll calculation – as it is and with the changes – in a database transaction that is always rolled back: no run, payslip, loan or advance deduction, approval or e-mail stays. Formula components (e.g. gratuity, housing as % of basic) follow the change by themselves; a formula component cannot be changed directly. The result shows gross pay now and with the change, the difference a month and a year, the net pay difference, and the difference by department, by salary component and per employee (CSV). **Apply to salaries** (users who may change employee salaries) writes the new amounts to the employees' salary components; each change is kept in the salary revision history with the scenario name and the month it applies from. An applied scenario is kept as the record and cannot be changed.

- New expense → choose the receipt → **Read the receipt**: the server reads the photo or PDF with Tesseract OCR (free, nothing is sent outside) and fills the amount, currency, date and merchant; VAT and the seller's TRN / VAT number are shown. The employee checks them before saving. The expense keeps what the receipt said.
- New checks on every expense (shown to the employee and the approver):
  - **Per month** limit of a category (Expense → Policies → category limits; warn or block);
  - **possible duplicate** – another expense of the same amount on the same day;
  - **the claim differs from the receipt** – the claimed amount is not what the receipt says.
- `expense/api/expenses/?flagged=1` lists the expenses with policy notes.

Expense → **Trips** is now the travel request: purpose, from / to, dates, travel by (air, car, train), class, **book a ticket** (or **use my air-ticket entitlement**), **book a hotel** (nights), per diem days, estimated cost and the advance. Approval follows the expense policy levels as before. When the trip is approved:
- the advance is made for finance to pay (as before);
- with *use my air-ticket entitlement*, an **air-ticket request** (type Ticket, linked to the employee's allocation, with the dates and places) goes through the air-ticket approvals;
- otherwise the trip is **to book**: the travel desk (users with *Can change trip*, else the company administrator) is told; it filters *Booking: to book* and presses **Book** with the reference (PNR / confirmation), cost and a note; the employee is told.

The **Trip journey** on each trip shows every step – requested, approved, advance, air ticket, booking, expenses (reports of the trip) and the settlement (what the company still pays or the employee returns of the advance).

Payroll → Payroll controls → **Payslip language**:
- *The reader's language* (as before);
- *English*;
- *English and Arabic on the same payslip* – every label in English on the left and Arabic on the right (company, period, employee, department, designation, branch, earnings, deductions, totals, net salary, signatures). Department / designation / branch / employee names use the Arabic translations (Settings → Translations); common salary components (basic, housing, transport, overtime, gratuity, loan …) have a built-in Arabic name.

Employees can always download the English + Arabic payslip in Self service → My payslips (**English + العربية**); `?lang=en_ar` on a payslip PDF link does the same.

Leave → Setup → **Leave conflicts**:
- *Warn when this many of the same role are away* (same designation in the same department, default 1);
- *Warn below this % of the department at work* (default 50 %);
- requests waiting for approval count as away (on / off);
- **Blackout periods**: name, dates, departments and branches (none = all), leave types they do not apply to (e.g. sick, emergency), *warn* or *block*, and a note to the employee. A blocking period refuses the employee's own request; HR can still enter leave.

When an employee applies (My leave, the kiosk), the form shows, before sending:
- the number of days;
- every rule the request breaks;
- colleagues of the same role who are away;
- department staffing below the minimum;
- the blackout period;
- rostered shifts without cover;
- a public holiday next to the leave.

The approver sees the same team conflict next to the roster conflict in Leave approvals. API: `leave-policy/api/check/`.

Settings → **WhatsApp, SMS and push**, off until switched on. The company brings its own account:
- **Twilio** (SMS or WhatsApp): account SID, auth token, sender.
- **WhatsApp Business Cloud API** (Meta): phone number ID, access token, and optionally an approved template with one body parameter. Business-initiated messages need a template.
- **Any HTTP gateway**: URL; ZEO POSTs JSON `{to, text, channel, sender}` with the key as a Bearer token.

The token is kept encrypted, and only its last 4 characters are shown. You choose what is sent:
- approvals waiting for me;
- decisions on my requests;
- payslip ready;
- answers from the HR helpdesk;
- every other notification.

The employee's first mobile number is used. Local numbers get the country code (default 971). *Send a test* sends one message now. The log keeps every message (sent / failed / skipped – no number).

Attendance → Kiosks → tick **Self-service** on the shared tablet of a labour camp or site. The kiosk page then has **My payslip and leave**. The employee signs in with the employee code or the Emirates ID / passport / labour card number, plus the kiosk PIN (the same PIN as for punching; employees with a login set it in My attendance, HR gives one to staff without a login in Attendance → **Kiosk PINs**, where a locked PIN is also unlocked). They can then:
- see the **leave balance** (and days waiting for approval) and the last leave requests;
- see the **payslips** with their lines and net pay;
- **ask for leave**, with the same check as My leave; the request goes through the normal leave request – rules, number, approvals;
- **ask HR** (a helpdesk ticket, channel *Kiosk*).

The session lasts 5 minutes and is renewed with every step. It is bound to the kiosk and nothing is kept on the tablet. The page signs out after 90 seconds without a touch, and 5 wrong PINs lock the PIN for 15 minutes.

- **Every user** can switch on the **authenticator app** in Settings → Users & rights → **My sign-in and out of office** (also by clicking the user name at the top):
  - scan the QR code with Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator or any TOTP app, or type the key;
  - type the code shown to switch it on;
  - keep the **10 recovery codes** – each signs in once if the phone is lost; new codes can be made with a code from the app.
- **Signing in** with the authenticator on: the password, then the 6-digit code (or a recovery code) – the e-mail code is not asked. A code works once; codes of the step before and after are accepted (phone clock off by up to 30 seconds). The same step is in the ZEO mobile app.
- **Company rules** (Settings → Users & rights → **Sign-in security**, company administrators):
  - minimum password length, a capital letter, a small letter, a digit, a symbol;
  - the password expires after … days, and cannot be one of the last … passwords;
  - lock after … wrong passwords for … minutes (also the e-mail and reset codes);
  - the authenticator app required for nobody, administrators, all staff users or everybody – users who must have it see a bar *Set it up* after signing in;
  - administrators may view ZEO as another user (on / off, see 71.6).

  A user of several companies follows the strictest rules of them. The rules apply when a user changes or resets a password (change password, forgot password, the employee reset).
- **Users** (same page): the authenticator on / off, locked, last sign-in and active sign-ins of each user, with *Unlock*, *Sign out* (everywhere) and *Reset authenticator*.

Settings → Administration → **System health** (company administrators) shows the state of each part, with what to do when it is not ok:
- the database (answer time, company data size), the cache, Celery workers and the scheduler (beat heartbeat every 5 minutes);
- the e-mail settings (*Test e-mail* connects to the server), free disk;
- the last backup (from `ZEO_BACKUP_DIR` / `ZEO_BACKUP_STATUS_FILE`), the licence, the version and database updates not applied;
- WhatsApp / SMS and push, webhooks failing, scheduled reports failing.

Reports → **Dashboards**:
- *New dashboard*, then *Change* → *Add a card*: a report (built-in or made with the report builder) shown as
  - a **number** (the number of rows, or the total of a number column);
  - **bars by a column** (the 12 largest, the rest as "Other");
  - **a line by month** of a date column (every month of the period);
  - **a short table** (the first rows).
- Each card has its own period (the report's own, this month, last month, this year, the last 12 months, the next 30 or 90 days), a size (small, wide, full width) and a title. Cards can be moved and removed.
- **Who sees it**: only me, everybody, or chosen permission groups. Every card runs as the person looking at it, so their rights apply and someone without the right sees a note instead of the figures.
- On every report, **Add to a dashboard** puts the report on one of your dashboards (or a new one) as a number, bars or a line.

Group → **Payroll in one currency** (group roles with the dashboard right):
- the gross pay, deductions, net pay and payslips of every company for the months chosen, in the company's own currency (the currency of the company, else of its country) and converted to the reporting currency of the group;
- the group total and gross pay by month.

The rate of the month comes from:
1. a rate entered for the group (1 KWD = … AED from a month on, until a later rate);
2. otherwise the opposite rate, inverted;
3. otherwise the US dollar pegs of the pegged currencies (AED 3.6725, SAR 3.75, QAR 3.64, OMR 0.3845, BHD 0.376, JOD 0.709).

The Kuwaiti dinar and the Indian rupee float, so they need a rate. A company without a rate is shown and flagged, but it is not added to the total.

Group owners and HR heads set the **reporting currency** and the **rates**. The group dashboard now shows each company's gross pay with its currency, and the group total converted to the reporting currency.

Settings → Administration → **Test company** (company administrators): a new company "<name> – test" made like any new company (same country, same apps), with the setup chosen from:
- branches, departments, designations and categories;
- leave types, leave policies, salary components, letter templates;
- form designs and extra fields;
- automation rules (copied switched off).

No employee, payroll, leave, attendance or request is copied. The test company is made safe: no e-mail leaves ZEO for it, the Projects mailbox is not read, and outside AI is off. The company's administrators get access, and *Open* switches to it.

*Delete* removes the test company and everything in it (only a company made here can be deleted this way). Permission groups are shared by every company of the server, so they need no copy. For a copy with the data, use *Duplicate* on the company list (1.22.3).

  - the same file, or the same number with the same expiry date → *Duplicate file*;
   - the same number with a later expiry → the existing document gets the new file and dates;
   - a new passport, visa, Emirates ID, labour card, driving licence or insurance card → the new one is current and the old one stays as history (inactive); an older one than the current → kept as history;
   - a number on another employee's document → *Conflict*.

**Check and import.** The grid shows every document with its file (click to open), the employee, type, number, dates, how each was found and the status (Ready, Needs review, Employee not found, Duplicate file, Conflict, Skipped). Choose the employee (code or name), type, number or dates of a row, or *Skip* it. **Import … ready documents** saves the ready rows; the others stay to be fixed. Options and follow-up:
- *Also update the identity details* (on by default) keeps the passport, visa, Emirates ID … numbers and dates of the employees in step.
- Expiry alerts are checked for the new documents at once.
- *Download the list (CSV)* gives every row with its status and reasons.
- The import is listed in Settings → **Import history**. *Undo* deletes the new documents, makes the replaced ones current again, gives the updated ones back their file and dates, and puts back the identity details.

Uploads wait in `staging/` (not under `media/`, which nginx serves without a login) and are removed when every row is imported or thrown away (*Upload another zip*), or after two days.

**HRMS › Employees › Exit › Leavers** replaces *Approved resignations*, *End of service* and *Final settlement* in the menu (their old addresses open Leavers).

- **The list:** every approved resignation, termination, end of contract, retirement and death – employee, branch, exit type, last working day, days left to the legal 14-day payment deadline (or "Paid on …"), net amount and a five-step stage: Resignation approved → End of service calculated → Checked by Finance → Approved → Paid. Count tiles filter the list (To calculate, With HR, With Finance, To approve, To pay, Paid); stage and branch filters, search, Excel / CSV.
- **New leaver:** termination, end of contract, retirement or death without a resignation request (approved at once – the employer's decision – and calculated straight away).
- **The case page:** service in years / months / days, unpaid days, notice, basic and wage; the statement with Earnings and Deductions, every line with its basis:
  - salary balance (days not yet paid by payroll, unpaid days deducted);
  - gratuity step by step (years × days × basic ÷ 30, the cap);
  - leave salary for unused days; notice pay or notice not served (HR can waive; none at end of contract);
  - air ticket: an approved allocation not used yet, and the ticket earned under the policy cycle when no allocation covers it (never twice);
  - each active loan's balance and salary advances not yet deducted;
  - assets still allocated, each returned / not returned – submitting waits until each is returned, recovered (amount deducted) or written off with a reason;
  - other additions and deductions added by HR (kept when the statement is recalculated).
  Net payable in figures and words, actions by role and stage (calculate, submit, Finance check, approve, mark paid with date

 list of this company);
`ZeoCloud/admin_alerts.py` (this company's administrators); `UserManagement/views.py` (domains of own companies, domains not
added by hand, company list of a "view as" = its company); `UserManagement/serializers.py` (`tenants` only the caller's
companies; company-wide notifications only for the caller's own record and only when the caller administers the company;
inbox only in the own record); `EmpManagement/views.py` (notification lists); `HRActions/views.py` (transfer inbox);
frontend My account: while viewing as, a note instead of the private blocks. Audit list and negative tests: see 130.T.
Migration: `ZeoCloud 0014_v1_67_6_signin_security` (non-core, public schema) – shared with item 13.

Every form of the 445 HRMS / Settings / Projects screens was checked field by field on the test company, then again as eleven
test users for the access rights. Code changes are marked `# v1.67.19 (…)` / `// v1.67.19 (…)`. No migrations;
`load_language_packs` adds the Arabic terms.

* **Settings › Data workbook › Download the demo workbook** gives *ZEO_Demo_Data_Desert_Palm_Trading.xlsx*: "Desert Palm Trading
  LLC", a fictional trading company. Every name, number and address in it is invented. It is made on the server from the client
  template, so its columns always match this version.
* What it makes:
  * two branches (Dubai head office DPT-DXB, Sharjah warehouse DPT-SHJ);
  * 14 employees with salaries, bank accounts (valid UAE IBANs), passports and Emirates IDs;
  * leave opening balances, family members, qualifications and job history;
  * logins for the 4 managers (user name = employee code, printed password slip);
  * a "Sales commission" component (COMM) entered each month as a monthly input.
* What it then works through, August – October 2026, through the screens' own API:
  * leave accrual on the 1st of each month;
  * 9 leave requests approved by the line managers (sick leave with its certificate);
  * the commission of the three sales executives;
  * the payroll of each branch, made by HR and approved by the finance manager (company administrator – segregation of duties);
  * the WPS salary file.
* It uses the masters a new company already has (Management, Finance, Human Resources, Sales, Logistics & Warehouse; General
  Manager, Accountant, Driver; Office Staff, Management) and adds only what it needs on top: one department, 7 designations,
  one category.
* Loading it twice is safe: the second load skips all 179 rows.
* Load it into a new, empty company with HR and Payroll on – not into a company with real data.
* API: `GET /tools/api/workbooks/demo/` (company administrators). Command: `python manage.py make_demo_workbook [--out file.xlsx]`.

* HR sends the new joiner a private link (no login), open for 3–90 days. A new link stops the old one.
* The candidate fills their details on the welcome page:
  * date of birth (18 or older), gender and marital status;
  * passport, Emirates ID, personal e-mail and phone;
  * addresses, the bank and IBAN (checked by mod-97), and an emergency contact.
* The candidate uploads the requested documents (PDF, JPG or PNG; up to 8 MB each; the file type is checked by its content).
* HR accepts the answers, or returns them with a note saying what to correct.
* When the employee is created from the offer, the accepted details go to the employee record:
  * the personal details and addresses;
  * the bank detail and the emergency contact;
  * the documents, with the passport number and expiry.
* API: `/recruitment/api/offers/<id>/preonboarding/` (HR) and `/recruitment/api/welcome/<token>/` (public).

* Each user gets a private ICS link for Google Calendar, Outlook or a phone calendar. It shows:
  * their own leave;
  * their team's approved leave;
  * public holidays;
  * the interviews they sit on.
* A new link stops the old one.

* Saves the incoming-webhook address of a Slack and/or a Teams channel. The addresses are kept encrypted, and only a masked form is shown again.
* Only Slack and Microsoft hosts are accepted. `ZEO_WEBHOOK_ALLOW_HOSTS` in `.env` adds other hosts.
* Events that can be ticked:
  * leave approved;
  * new joiner;
  * announcement;
  * payroll approved (no amounts);
  * new helpdesk question (number and category only).
* A message is sent after the transaction commits. A failure never stops the business action, and the last result is shown on the page.

* The company administrator enters an address, e.g. `hr.yourcompany.com`, and adds a CNAME record pointing to the ZEO server's host (the host of `ZEO_APP_URL`), or an A record to the server's IP address.
* **Check** verifies the DNS.
* After that, the sign-in page at that address shows the company and opens it directly.
* **Server administrator, once per domain:**
  1. add the name to the nginx `server_name` line, or use a catch-all server block;
  2. issue a TLS certificate for it (e.g. `certbot --nginx -d hr.yourcompany.com`);
  3. add the name to `ZEO_ALLOWED_HOSTS` and `https://<name>` to `ZEO_CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` in `.env`;
  4. restart gunicorn.

* Your own registers without programming. For each register you set:
  * its fields (text, number, date, choice, yes/no, employee);
  * who may add records and who sees them;
  * a number prefix;
  * the Blueprint: the states a record goes through and, for each move, who may make it (owner, manager, HR, administrator or a permission group), the fields it needs and whether a note is required.
* Every move is kept in the record's history.
* Users find the registers under **Custom modules** in the menu.

* A salary review against a budget (% of the basic salaries):
  * fill the cycle with the employees (optionally only those who joined before a date, and with their appraisal ratings);
  * propose a % per employee and send for approval;
  * a different person approves (the preparer cannot);
  * apply from one date: the basic salary line gets a new valid-from;
  * issue increment letters.
* **Self service › Mail merge** (HR):
  * one letter template for many employees;
  * each employee gets their own letter (reference number, verification code, PDF), optionally by e-mail;
  * all the letters download in one ZIP.
* New letter types: increment and general.

* **Settings › Teams and Slack › A channel per branch (optional):** a branch can have its own Slack and/or Teams channel.
* The events of that branch go to the branch's channel instead of the company channel:
  * leave approved;
  * new joiner;
  * new HR helpdesk question;
  * a payroll run or announcement of exactly that branch.
* A branch without its own channel uses the company channel.
* "Send a test" checks each branch channel.
* Remove = back to the company channel.
* The addresses are kept encrypted and shown masked, like the company channel.

* The service charge collected in a month and branch is shared among the branch's active employees in one of three ways:
  * by points (per designation or per employee);
  * by days worked (attendance);
  * equally.
* The rounding cent goes to the largest share, so the shares add up to the pool exactly.
* "Send to payroll" writes each share as monthly input ZSVC.

* **Per employee:** the MOHRE skill level, Nafis registration and number, and Nafis salary support with its end date. These are for UAE nationals only.
* **Quota:**
  * the skilled workforce (the skill levels that count – 1, 2, 3 by default);
  * the Emiratis in skilled jobs;
  * the number required by the target HR enters from MOHRE's notice (for 20 – 49 employee companies, a minimum number);
  * how many are still to hire;
  * the monthly and yearly contribution at the amount HR enters.
* The page notes the 2026 rule as published:
  * 2 % a year (1 % each half year);
  * AED 10,000 a month (AED 120,000 a year) per Emirati not hired, from 1 July 2026.
  * Sources: Gulf News; Emirates 24|7.

* **Setup:** a name; a fixed amount, a % of the basic or a % of the gross; an optional maximum; the number of instalments (within Payroll › Loan and advance settings). It can go to every employee or to chosen ones.
