```bash
cd /opt/zeo/zeo-hrms
/opt/zeo/venv/bin/python manage.py migrate_schemas --shared          # shared tables (up to 15 minutes on a small server)
/opt/zeo/venv/bin/python manage.py setup_zeo \
    --company "Your Company LLC" --admin-username admin --admin-email admin@yourcompany.com \
    --branch "Head office" --branch-code HO --uae-leave --expense-defaults \
    --industry PM --apps hrms,payroll,projects,crm,property,maintenance,hse
```
`--industry` is the company industry type: IT, HC, FIN, EDU, MFG, CON (construction), OG (oil and gas), PM (property management), RET or OTH (General). Each app starts with the industry that matches it. `--apps` lists the apps the company uses (default `hrms,projects`; add `payroll` for the payroll screens). Running `setup_zeo` again only switches on the apps it names – it never switches an app off (1.56.1). You can change both later in **Settings → Apps** (1.21.0).

For a company outside the UAE add `--country "Saudi Arabia"` (any country name from the list). The currency and time zone follow the country.

`setup_zeo` does the following:
- loads the shared master data: 55 countries, the 7 emirates, GCC regions, currencies, nationalities, religions, languages and VAT rates;
- creates the public tenant and the administrator. It asks for the password, which must be at least 10 characters;
- creates the company, which gets its own schema with all its tables (up to 15 minutes on a small server), and its first branch;
- loads the UAE leave types and the Office / Labour leave policies;
- loads the expense categories and a default expense policy;
- loads the **country defaults** of the company's country (document types, labour-law rule set, weekend, leave types when there are none). Skip with `--no-country-defaults`;
- activates the app

